\newlabel{fig:teaser}{{1}{2}{Stage-3 feature trajectories of a weight-tied ConvNeXt (left) and a standard ConvNeXt-T (right), integrated with Euler up to $T{=}9$ ($\Delta t{=}0.09$ and $\Delta t{=}0.01$; massive channel removed; $200$ ImageNet validation images). \textbf {Top:} states are flattened and mapped to $2048$ dimensions with a fixed Gaussian random projection \citep {johnson1984extensions,dasgupta2003elementary}, and PCA is fitted on all projected states of each model \citep {halko2011finding}; paths coloured by depth $t$, white dots mark integer $t$. \textbf {Bottom:} residual speed $\|f(x(t))\|$ (mean over images; shade: P10--P90). One shared block is a single autonomous field $\dot x = f(x)$; nine independent blocks switch the field at every integer, $\dot x = f_{\lfloor t\rfloor }(x)$. We analyse this contrast throughout the paper}{figure.1}{}}
