\newlabel{fig:kinematics-compare}{{6}{10}{Stage-3 kinematics over $T{=}9$ ($R{=}100$, Euler $\Delta t{=}0.01$; massive channel ignored; mean and P5--P95 over $N{=}500$). \textbf {Top:} weight-tied ConvNeXt. \textbf {Bottom:} untied ConvNeXt-T. Columns: velocity $\|v\|$, angular velocity $\omega $, acceleration decomposition $(\|a\|,a_t,a_n)$, curvature $\kappa {=}a_n/\|v\|^2$. The shared field traces a smooth three-phase arc; the untied stack is piecewise within each block. On the untied row, pairs that straddle a block boundary are omitted from $\omega $, $a$ and $\kappa $: there $v$ is discontinuous, so finite differences diverge as $\Delta t\!\to \!0$ and are not representative of the within-block dynamics}{figure.6}{}}
\newlabel{fig:kinematics-compare@cref}{{[figure][6][]6}{[1][9][]10}}
\newlabel{sec:beyond_horizon}{{3.3.5}{10}{}{subsubsection.3.3.5}{}}
